From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Grische <github@grische.xyz>
Date: Tue, 1 Sep 2026 17:17:09 +0200
Subject: MIPS: dts: intel-mips: drop the PCIe controllers' clock-names

Each root complex has exactly one clock and pcie-intel-gw.c looks it up
unnamed, so the name says nothing the node does not already say. It is
also not a name the DesignWare common schema recognises: "ctl" is neither
one of the generic clock names nor one of the vendor names that schema
grandfathers, so a binding for this node cannot describe the property
without asking for an exception for a string nothing reads.

intel,lgm-pcie, the other user of this driver, names no clock either.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5
Signed-off-by: Grische <github@grische.xyz>

diff --git a/arch/mips/boot/dts/intel-mips/xrx500.dtsi b/arch/mips/boot/dts/intel-mips/xrx500.dtsi
index ca9ee9de2c6b..5654e6b771a6 100644
--- a/arch/mips/boot/dts/intel-mips/xrx500.dtsi
+++ b/arch/mips/boot/dts/intel-mips/xrx500.dtsi
@@ -317,7 +317,6 @@ pcie0: pcie@18900000 {
 				<0 0 0 4 &gic GIC_SHARED 139 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_HIGH>;
 
 		clocks = <&cgu GCLK_PCIE0>;
-		clock-names = "ctl";
 		phys = <&pcie_phy0>;
 		phy-names = "pcie";
 
@@ -352,7 +351,6 @@ pcie1: pcie@18400000 {
 				<0 0 0 4 &gic GIC_SHARED 12 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_HIGH>;
 
 		clocks = <&cgu GCLK_PCIE1>;
-		clock-names = "ctl";
 		phys = <&pcie_phy1>;
 		phy-names = "pcie";
 
@@ -387,7 +385,6 @@ pcie2: pcie@18e00000 {
 				<0 0 0 4 &gic GIC_SHARED 158 IRQ_TYPE_LEVEL_HIGH>;
 
 		clocks = <&cgu GCLK_PCIE2>;
-		clock-names = "ctl";
 		phys = <&pcie_phy2>;
 		phy-names = "pcie";
 
